[{:db/id "4bc4984a-76a7-5e40-bec6-4baeb697eb93" :answer/id #uuid "4bc4984a-76a7-5e40-bec6-4baeb697eb93" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{17}{8}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "b382a9d0-fd0f-530d-8c12-c535c8651899" :answer/id #uuid "b382a9d0-fd0f-530d-8c12-c535c8651899" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{15}{17}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "c8cc011f-2ad6-5dc2-af67-11ebde52edbe" :answer/id #uuid "c8cc011f-2ad6-5dc2-af67-11ebde52edbe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{8}{17}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "93b2d161-28c4-50ff-962d-90ee2fbdac17" :answer/id #uuid "93b2d161-28c4-50ff-962d-90ee2fbdac17" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{15}{8}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "a332604f-d236-5a81-8925-b96c1993b9c4" :answer/id #uuid "a332604f-d236-5a81-8925-b96c1993b9c4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{8}{15}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "68af0948-d377-54ba-bc95-3bf16b5f82fd" :answer-field/id #uuid "68af0948-d377-54ba-bc95-3bf16b5f82fd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["4bc4984a-76a7-5e40-bec6-4baeb697eb93" "b382a9d0-fd0f-530d-8c12-c535c8651899" "c8cc011f-2ad6-5dc2-af67-11ebde52edbe" "93b2d161-28c4-50ff-962d-90ee2fbdac17" "a332604f-d236-5a81-8925-b96c1993b9c4"] :answer-field/correct "93b2d161-28c4-50ff-962d-90ee2fbdac17" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "cab2c352-408a-5716-9c82-d09e82069fc3" :question/id #uuid "cab2c352-408a-5716-9c82-d09e82069fc3" :question/problem "![](images/dd/dd9061a8ef1b2f0d8fe9d730f18c5e10bef42a9acd33f23d36efb3728ce0614b.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the unit circle. Given that the $y$-coordinate of the point $P$ is $\\frac{15}{17},$ use the Pythagorean identity to find $tan⁡\\theta .$" :question/worked-solution "![](images/ba/bad705982f073623644ed540e26cfad849b2dd078c5c64772a0be3937d618a27.png)\n\nAny point $(x,y)$ on the unit circle is related to the central angle $\\theta $ as follows:\n\n$$\nx=cos⁡\\theta ,\\,y=sin⁡\\theta \n$$\n\nWe're given that $y=\\frac{15}{17}$ at the point $P.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\nsin⁡\\theta =\\frac{15}{17}.\n$$\n\nWe can use the Pythagorean identity to find $cos⁡\\theta :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta  & =1 \\\\ {cos}^{2}⁡\\theta  & =1-{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\ cos⁡\\theta  & =\\pm \\sqrt{1-{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $sin⁡\\theta =\\frac{15}{17}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}cos⁡\\theta  & =\\pm \\sqrt{1-{(\\frac{15}{17})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{1-\\frac{225}{289}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{64}{289}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{8}{17}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe select the positive answer since $cos⁡\\theta $ is positive in the first quadrant. So, $cos⁡\\theta =\\frac{8}{17}.$\n\nFinally, knowing that $tan⁡\\theta =\\frac{sin⁡\\theta }{cos⁡\\theta },$ we have\n\n$$\ntan⁡\\theta =\\frac{(\\frac{15}{17})}{(\\frac{8}{17})}=\\frac{15}{8}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["68af0948-d377-54ba-bc95-3bf16b5f82fd"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "ec9189a3-d0b3-5483-9c84-198750079c85" :answer/id #uuid "ec9189a3-d0b3-5483-9c84-198750079c85" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{58}}{7}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "f7e48c42-ff53-5bcc-b008-e6ccbde37ace" :answer/id #uuid "f7e48c42-ff53-5bcc-b008-e6ccbde37ace" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{19}}{7}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "2fc3517e-1300-5538-b247-d948b579f7f3" :answer/id #uuid "2fc3517e-1300-5538-b247-d948b579f7f3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{14}}{6}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "1909811c-da8d-539b-aa89-cdc5b420a83f" :answer/id #uuid "1909811c-da8d-539b-aa89-cdc5b420a83f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{7}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "f3b2d445-8bcf-5fd5-a74d-dc7c7c42cc23" :answer/id #uuid "f3b2d445-8bcf-5fd5-a74d-dc7c7c42cc23" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3\\sqrt{14}}{7}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "c5c54992-c621-521f-8066-259a4e4e6c43" :answer-field/id #uuid "c5c54992-c621-521f-8066-259a4e4e6c43" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["ec9189a3-d0b3-5483-9c84-198750079c85" "f7e48c42-ff53-5bcc-b008-e6ccbde37ace" "2fc3517e-1300-5538-b247-d948b579f7f3" "1909811c-da8d-539b-aa89-cdc5b420a83f" "f3b2d445-8bcf-5fd5-a74d-dc7c7c42cc23"] :answer-field/correct "f3b2d445-8bcf-5fd5-a74d-dc7c7c42cc23" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "3c08d8db-de56-5ccc-8319-0573cd7cc4f0" :question/id #uuid "3c08d8db-de56-5ccc-8319-0573cd7cc4f0" :question/problem "![](images/d0/d04fe72eb2ad53b69837aaf402addd75d9b087225d70e876233e23092fc85764.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the unit circle. Given that the $y$-coordinate of the point $P$ is $\\frac{\\sqrt{18}}{5},$ use the Pythagorean identity to find $tan⁡\\theta .$" :question/worked-solution "![](images/51/51778a4029b91dbbd51014a8f4a3e7e1fc772efe96058f41b21bbf408f113cce.png)\n\nAny point $(x,y)$ on the unit circle is related to the central angle $\\theta $ as follows:\n\n$$\nx=cos⁡\\theta ,\\,y=sin⁡\\theta \n$$\n\nWe're given that $y=\\frac{\\sqrt{18}}{5}$ at the point $P.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\nsin⁡\\theta =\\frac{\\sqrt{18}}{5}.\n$$\n\nWe can use the Pythagorean identity to find $cos⁡\\theta :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta  & =1 \\\\ {cos}^{2}⁡\\theta  & =1-{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\ cos⁡\\theta  & =\\pm \\sqrt{1-{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $sin⁡\\theta =\\frac{\\sqrt{18}}{5}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}cos⁡\\theta  & =\\pm \\sqrt{1-{(\\frac{\\sqrt{18}}{5})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{1-\\frac{18}{25}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{7}{25}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe select the positive answer since $cos⁡\\theta $ is positive in the first quadrant. So, $cos⁡\\theta =\\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{5}.$\n\nKnowing that $tan⁡\\theta =\\frac{sin⁡\\theta }{cos⁡\\theta },$ we have\n\n$$\ntan⁡\\theta =\\frac{(\\frac{\\sqrt{18}}{5})}{(\\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{5})}=\\frac{\\sqrt{18}}{\\sqrt{7}}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we rationalize the denominator.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}tan⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{18}}{\\sqrt{7}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{18}}{\\sqrt{7}}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{\\sqrt{7}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{18\\cdot 7}}{7} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{126}}{7}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["c5c54992-c621-521f-8066-259a4e4e6c43"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "ed349bbe-0002-555d-b774-e4baa909f28c" :answer/id #uuid "ed349bbe-0002-555d-b774-e4baa909f28c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{79}}{10}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "f51c1080-9d67-5d5c-9ad2-f5bee4c4e810" :answer/id #uuid "f51c1080-9d67-5d5c-9ad2-f5bee4c4e810" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{10}}{5}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "19cd8750-e5e7-52ce-b115-cbd111d3d902" :answer/id #uuid "19cd8750-e5e7-52ce-b115-cbd111d3d902" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{390}}{39}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "dca87888-b247-5218-bd97-b52279791479" :answer/id #uuid "dca87888-b247-5218-bd97-b52279791479" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{39}}{10}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "5ba5953e-1bc3-52b3-949b-b1a3372ec514" :answer/id #uuid "5ba5953e-1bc3-52b3-949b-b1a3372ec514" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{390}}{10}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "89a72e76-dfbf-51a2-96d4-d8c440244cee" :answer-field/id #uuid "89a72e76-dfbf-51a2-96d4-d8c440244cee" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["ed349bbe-0002-555d-b774-e4baa909f28c" "f51c1080-9d67-5d5c-9ad2-f5bee4c4e810" "19cd8750-e5e7-52ce-b115-cbd111d3d90